     Paths are relative to this file. Update it when the layout changes. -->

| | |
|---|---|
| **SPA source** | `[TODO: e.g. ./spa/src]` |
| **Backend repo** | `[TODO: e.g. ./jam/education]` |
| **Component library (Storybook)** | `[TODO: e.g. http://localhost:5600/component-library]` |
| **Backend API spec** | `[TODO: OpenAPI/Swagger path or URL, e.g. ./jam/education/swagger.yaml]` |
| **Claude Design project** | `[TODO: claude.ai/design design-system project name or ID]` |

Commands resolve the API contract **spec-first** (the OpenAPI/Swagger document is the
published contract; routes/controllers in the backend repo are the fallback and the
cross-check) and the component catalog from the **component library** URL
(`<url>/index.json`). The **Claude Design project** is where `/frontend:design-sync`
publishes the component catalog and where approved feature designs
(`designs/<feature>/manifest.json`) are read from. If an entry is missing or still
`[TODO]`, commands ask the operator and offer to fill it in here. Default topology when
unset: SPA and backend as sibling repos at the same folder level.

```
/frontend:discover → /frontend:analyze-patterns → /frontend:plan-feature
    → /frontend:decompose → build → /frontend:code-structure → /frontend:review-loop
                                        ↘ /engineer:create-pr → /engineer:review-pr → /engineer:pr-review-loop
                                        ↘ /engineer:handoff (before clearing)
```

| Command | Phase | Does |
|---|---|---|
| `/frontend:discover` | Discovery | Views/routes, components, state, backend contract; refuses to code |
| `/frontend:analyze-patterns` | Plan | Extract CRUD/component patterns from disk + Storybook; ask which to adopt; write `plan/<feature>.patterns.md` |
| `/frontend:plan-feature` | Plan | Risk-first plan: module layout, components, store, service/ACL layer |
| `/frontend:decompose` | Plan | Split into stacked story branches (types → service → store → views) |
| `/frontend:code-structure` | Build | Component split, composables, service layer, DDD module isolation |
| `/frontend:review-loop` | Review | Review (reactivity, a11y, library-first, tests) → fix → re-test until green |
| `/frontend:enterprise-review` | Review | Same deep principles audit as `/engineer:enterprise-review`, frontend expressions |
| `/frontend:design-sync` | Design | Publish the component catalog to the Claude Design project (incremental; Claude Code only) |

PR flow and handoff reuse the `engineer:` commands. In Cursor the same commands are flat
with a prefix: `/frontend-discover`, `/frontend-analyze-patterns`, … Frontend standards:
`.cursor/rules/frontend-standards.mdc`. Subagents: `frontend-planner`, `frontend-reviewer`,
`pattern-analyst`.

## Agents
Subagents (`planner`, `researcher`, `reviewer`, `pr-reviewer`) are available for
specialised work — in Claude Code they load natively from `.claude/agents/`; in Cursor
from the installed plugin. See `AGENTS.md` for when to use each.

## Hooks
Three guardrails (`dep-age-guard`, `format-changed`, `run-tests`) run automatically:
- **Claude Code:** wired in `.claude/settings.json`, scripts at `.claude/hooks/`.
- **Cursor:** from the **installed plugin**; `.cursor/hooks/` symlinks are reference only.
See `HOOKS.md` for when each fires and what it does.

## MCP
A GitHub MCP server config (`github`) ships with the workflow:
- **Claude Code:** `.mcp.json` at the repo root (copied by bootstrap; approve on first use).
- **Cursor:** loads from the **installed plugin**; reference symlink at
  `.cursor/agentic-workflow-mcp.json`.
See `MCP.md` for servers and required env vars.

## Not in this plugin
Cursor skills (`~/.cursor/skills-cursor/`) are a separate system — not symlinked or
referenced here. This workflow uses plugin **commands**, **agents**, **hooks**, and **MCP**
only.

